---
/**
 * Google Analytics, on the marketing site only.
 *
 * The app measures itself in our own Postgres and deliberately ships no
 * analytics SDK (`docs/analytics.md`). That decision was about the app, and
 * the same document says counting strangers "lives with the website, not the
 * app backend" — which is this file. Nothing here runs on a phone, and no
 * signed-in user is identified by it.
 *
 * **Consent Mode, defaulting to denied.** With `analytics_storage` denied,
 * gtag sends cookieless pings: no cookie is set, so there is nothing a consent
 * banner would be asking permission for. That is worth more than the returning
 * visitor identity it costs. The site's whole pitch on the tool pages is that
 * nothing is stored, and a cookie wall in front of that sentence would be a
 * poor way to make it.
 *
 * **Host-gated rather than build-gated.** Vercel builds a preview deployment
 * for every push and `astro dev` serves the same pages on localhost; both
 * would otherwise report into the same property as the real site. Checking the
 * hostname at runtime catches both with one condition, and keeps this file
 * byte-identical to the copies in the three static pages — which is what makes
 * `analytics.test.ts` a string comparison rather than a parser.
 *
 * **The copies.** `privacy.html`, `terms.html` and `delete-account.html` own
 * their own `<head>` and cannot import this. They carry the same script inline.
 * The test globs `pages/*.html`, so a new one fails on the day it is added.
 */
---

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    if (location.hostname !== 'www.flintroom.app') return;

    var id = 'G-Q1GZBK57YS';

    window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
    function gtag() { window.dataLayer.push(arguments); }
    window.gtag = gtag;

    gtag('consent', 'default', {
      ad_storage: 'denied',
      ad_user_data: 'denied',
      ad_personalization: 'denied',
      analytics_storage: 'denied'
    });

    gtag('js', new Date());
    gtag('config', id);

    var tag = document.createElement('script');
    tag.async = true;
    tag.src = 'https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=' + id;
    document.head.appendChild(tag);
  })();
</script>
